OL,3,GUK long range forecast                 
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 23 Nov to Wed 2 Dec    
OL,6,FBands of rain will move in from the    
OL,7,FAtlantic at times, making erratic and  
OL,8,Funcertain eastward progress across the 
OL,9,FUK. These systems may also bring       
OL,10,Foccasional strong winds. Either side   
OL,11,Fof bands of rain a mixture of clear/   
OL,12,Fsunny spells and showers. Often rather 
OL,13,Fcold in northern areas which could     
OL,14,Fallow precipitation to fall as snow at 
OL,15,Ftimes, mainly over hills. Generally    
OL,16,Fmilder in the south though still       
OL,17,Fpotential for some cold nights in      
OL,18,Fclearer spells. Through late November, 
OL,19,Fthere is an increasing chance that     
OL,20,Fhigh pressure will start to have more  
OL,21,Finfluence bringing more settled        
OL,22,Fconditions, particularly across the    
OL,23,Fnorth, with southern areas remainingice
OL,24,Fmore prone to milder and wetter FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,0,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
PS,C000
CT,20,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 163 Wed 18 NovC15:48/33
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3 
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast                 
OL,5,COutlook for Thu 3 Dec to Thu 17 DecFThe
OL,6,Ftrack of low pressure systems will     
OL,7,Flikely be further south than normal    
OL,8,Fduring this period. This means that    
OL,9,Frainfall will probably be focused      
OL,10,Facross the south of the UK with a risk 
OL,11,Fof stronger winds at times;            
OL,12,Fconversely, higher pressure developing 
OL,13,Fto the north means drier and more      
OL,14,Fsettled conditions are more likely     
OL,15,Fhere. Temperatures in the south will   
OL,16,Fprobably be near normal or perhaps     
OL,17,Fslightly above at times, with the      
OL,18,Fnorth colder than normal, although     
OL,19,Feither bias could extended to cover a  
OL,20,Fwider area of the UK at times.         
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
